cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  variant-fm-benchmark: calibration and fusion of splice and sequence-based
  variant-effect predictors benchmarked against saturation genome editing
  functional assays
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the software
  (this file) and the accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Ningyi
    affiliation: Department of Biological Sciences, National University of Singapore
    email: cliffzhang@u.nus.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3020-4044"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oneone00-11/variant-fm-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Evidence strength of splice-region variant effect predictors against
  saturation genome editing functional assays in seven hereditary-cancer genes
  (BRCA1, BRCA2, BARD1, PALB2, RAD51C, VHL, BAP1): the published SpliceAI cut
  points of the ClinGen splicing recommendation, predictor-specific interval
  calibration of PP3/BP4 likelihood ratios under leave-one-gene-out evaluation,
  and transfer to two genes outside the seven (DDX3X and TP53).
keywords:
  - variant effect prediction
  - saturation genome editing
  - splice prediction
  - calibration
  - ACMG evidence strength
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
